  "changes": [
    "Operation/ID-range/aggregate workspace reservation and queue publication hold the endpoint gate; caller-thread encoding/allocation/native Future creation run outside it.",
    "Successful pre-Close reservations can publish ACCEPTED afterward and are completed without send; failed construction refunds all resource credits but consumes its never-reused ID range.",
    "Constructor references cover close/publication/rollback; closing with only physical pins remaining has a retry hint for a Wake before final retirement.",
    "Private 21-byte comparison keys replace per-entry 4096-byte slots for the only locally generated string IDs; full response validation, escaped semantic equality, unknown long IDs and original retained response bytes are preserved.",
    "Info exposes Constructing/TemporaryBytes/PeakTemporaryBytes; old consumer structs must be recompiled for checked Size/layout change."
  ],
